WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.664
Log in. Download. Copy. Paste. Send.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.697
Every week, the same clicks.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.047
What if you only had to explain it once?

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.117
Just tell Kitewell what you do, in plain words.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.381
It lays out every step, for you to check.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:33.840
Then it does the clicking — on websites, desktop apps, and email.

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:36.652
Even the old app nothing else can talk to.

00:00:37.450 --> 00:00:40.200
It stops for your OK where it matters.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:42.195
And it keeps a record of every step.

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.760
It learns the clicks once.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:52.587
After that, it repeats them every weekday — without paying for AI each time.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.450
Prefer code? It's plain YAML underneath.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:01.560
Run scripts, containers, and coding agents like Claude Code and Codex.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:04.666
Or build it all from your own agent, over MCP.

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.330
And it all runs on your own computer.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:11.501
Share workflows with your team — your passwords stay on your machine.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:13.012
Kitewell.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.980
It flies on its own.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.246
You hold the string.
